    "id": "lem:relative-interior-tangent-lift",
    "kind": "lemma",
    "statement": "Suppose \\(p_0\\in\\operatorname{relint}(\\mathcal P_{\\mathrm{ASC}})\\) and \\(\\operatorname{im}(B)\\subseteq\\operatorname{lin}(\\mathcal P_{\\mathrm{ASC}}-p_0)\\).  For every \\(u\\in\\mathbb R^d\\) there is \\(t_u>0\\) such that\n\\[\n p_0+tBu\\in\\mathcal P_{\\mathrm{ASC}}\n \\qquad\\text{for every }0\\le t\\le t_u.\n\\]\nFor rational \\(u\\), a positive rational \\(t_u\\) is computable from the rational relative-facet representation, and for every rational \\(t\\in[0,t_u]\\) a rational response-type lift \\(\\lambda(t,u)\\in\\Xi(p_0+tBu)\\) is computable.  Thus every tangent direction has a compatible full-law lift; feasibility is derived and is not assumed on an ambient simplex neighborhood.",
    "free_symbols": [
      "PASC",
      "pZero",
      "Bmap",
      "u",
      "d",
      "XiFiber",
      "Ffiber"
    ],
    "depends_on": [
      "def:compatible-observed-law-polytope",
      "lem:compatible-observed-law-polytope",
      "prop:fiber-polytope-equivalence"
    ],
    "proof_tex": "Use the rational relative representation from the compatible-observed-law-polytope lemma,\n\\[\n \\mathcal P_{\\mathrm{ASC}}=\\{q:Eq=e,\\ F_iq\\le f_i,\\ i\\in I\\}.\n\\]\nPut \\(L=\\operatorname{lin}(\\mathcal P_{\\mathrm{ASC}}-p_0)=\\ker E\\) and \\(v=Bu\\).  The image condition gives \\(v\\in L\\), hence\n\\[\n E(p_0+tv)=Ep_0+tEv=e \\qquad(t\\in\\mathbb R). \\tag{5}\n\\]\nRelative interior gives a strictly positive slack\n\\[\n \\gamma_i=f_i-F_ip_0>0\\qquad(i\\in I). \\tag{6}\n\\]\nWith the minimum over an empty set interpreted as \\(+\\infty\\), define\n\\[\n t_u=\\min\\left\\{1,\\ \\min_{i:F_iv>0}\\frac{\\gamma_i}{2F_iv}\\right\\}>0. \\tag{7}\n\\]\nIf \\(0\\le t\\le t_u\\) and \\(F_iv>0\\), then (6)--(7) give\n\\[\n F_i(p_0+tv)\n =f_i-\\gamma_i+tF_iv\n \\le f_i-\\frac{\\gamma_i}{2}<f_i. \\tag{8}\n\\]\nIf \\(F_iv\\le0\\), then\n\\[\n F_i(p_0+tv)\\le F_ip_0=f_i-\\gamma_i<f_i. \\tag{9}\n\\]\nEquations (5), (8), and (9) prove \\(p_0+tBu\\in\\mathcal P_{\\mathrm{ASC}}\\).  By the defining equality \\(\\mathcal P_{\\mathrm{ASC}}=\\{q:\\mathcal F(q)\\ne\\varnothing\\}\\) and the established fiber-polytope equivalence, there exists \\(\\lambda(t,u)\\in\\Xi(p_0+tBu)\\), and its response-type construction induces a law in \\(\\mathcal F(p_0+tBu)\\).  When \\(u\\) and \\(t\\) are rational, all constraints have rational coefficients, and exact rational linear programming returns a basic feasible \\(\\lambda(t,u)\\).  Formula (7) supplies the computable rational upper step.  This is the promised computable lift.",
